// Puzzle data for Warmer, the daily semantic hot-and-cold word hunt. Imported
// ONLY by the server page (app/warmer/page.js), which filters live<=today and
// passes ONLY the active day's packed `o` to the client — so future answers
// never ship to the browser.
//
// Each puzzle stores `o`: the VOCAB indices sorted by cosine similarity to that
// day's secret answer, most-similar FIRST, packed three base64 characters per
// index (see ./order-codec.js). `board()` hangs a lazy `p.order` off it that
// decodes to the same array this file used to spell out, so order[0] is the
// answer's own index (VOCAB[p.order[0]] === the answer). The client turns a
// guess into a rank by finding its position there; rank 1 wins. The answer is
// never stored as a string. Similarities computed on GloVe-6B-100d native
// vectors (July 2026 rebuild; the old word2vec + WordNet-bridge orders are
// retired). Generated by scripts/gen-warmer.mjs, verified by
// scripts/verify-warmer.mjs.
//
// STORAGE, not content, changed on 2026-09-05. The bank used to write each
// order as 32,300 numeric literals; at 136 boards that is 4.4 million AST nodes
// in a module five other server modules import for its dates alone, and
// `next build` was SIGKILLed parsing it. The packed form is 136 string literals
// for the identical data — every board decodes element-for-element to what
// shipped before. Do not "simplify" it back to arrays.
import { board } from './order-codec.js';

